+* `value` - the cell-weighted mean clonal entropy over the pair. With only two categories it runs from 0 to 1. A `0` means the clones making up the anchor cluster are exclusive to it. A `1` means every clone in the anchor is split evenly with the partner.
+
+Two rows exist for each pair because each cluster takes a turn as the anchor. They usually differ, and that asymmetry comes from the weighting rather than from any direction of travel. A pair labeled `1 vs 3` is not a claim that cells moved from cluster 1 to cluster 3.
+
+This matters if you are grouping by time point. STARTRAC describes clonal sharing as it stands, so it cannot order that sharing in time on its own. To ask whether a clone moved from a cluster at t1 into a different cluster at t2, track clone identity across the time points directly, for example with `alluvialClones()` or by tabulating each clone's cluster membership per time point.
+
 ## clonalBias
 
 A new metric proposed by [Massimo et al](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35829695/), ```clonalBias()```, like STARTRAC, is a clonal metric that seeks to quantify how individual clones are skewed towards a specific cellular compartment or cluster. A clone bias of `1` indicates that a clone is composed of cells from a single compartment or cluster, while a clone bias of `0` matches the background subtype distribution. Please read and cite the linked manuscript if using `clonalBias()`
